dArkOS: Select and the black screensaver.
- ES starts its screensaver when Select is let go (SystemView), and any input
  ends it. On a dark screen a press of Select lit it, and its release started
  the screensaver again: the screen was lit only while Select was held. The
  release of the press that woke the screen (cancelled the screensaver, or woke
  ES from sleep) is now part of that wake-up and goes nowhere else.
- The black screensaver read the brightness back only when it stopped, with the
  backlight off by then, and put back an older level, if any. It keeps the level
  it found when it starts now.
- brightnessctl ran in the background ("&"): the screensaver started and stopped
  within a fraction of a second, its "0%" could finish after the level put back,
  and the screen stayed dark with the screensaver over. It runs in the
  foreground now (-q), so that two in a row are applied in order.

--- a/es-core/src/Window.cpp
